    {
      "box": [
        48.7388916015625,
        137.384765625,
        328.08782958984375,
        147.86264038085938
      ],
      "text": "14\nWhat is the writer’s main point in the first paragraph?\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        71.96345520019531,
        157.3382568359375,
        357.1481628417969,
        167.81619262695312
      ],
      "text": "A\nOur use of technology is having a hidden effect on us.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.61766815185547,
        170.09544372558594,
        346.98651123046875,
        180.90074157714844
      ],
      "text": "B_\nTechnology can be used to help youngsters to read.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.61763763427734,
        183.1796875,
        397.77459716796875,
        193.65756225585938
      ],
      "text": "C_\nTravellers should be encouraged to use technology on planes.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.61760711669922,
        195.93687438964844,
        411.5522766113281,
        206.74217224121094
      ],
      "text": "D_\nPlaying games is a more popular use of technology than reading.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        48.73883056640625,
        221.77828979492188,
        402.157958984375,
        253.84812927246094
      ],
      "text": "15\nWhat main point does Sherry Turkle make about innovation?\nA__ Technological innovation has led to a reduction in print reading.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.6175765991211,
        254.81607055664062,
        464.7007141113281,
        278.0511169433594
      ],
      "text": "B_\nWe should pay attention to what might be lost when innovation occurs.\nC\n Weshould encourage more young people to become involved in innovation.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.94464874267578,
        280.657470703125,
        451.56402587890625,
        291.1353759765625
      ],
      "text": "D_\nThere is a difference between developing products and developing ideas.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        49.06584548950195,
        306.17181396484375,
        342.57855224609375,
        316.97711181640625
      ],
      "text": "16\nWhat point is the writer making in the fourth paragraph?\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.29041290283203,
        326.452392578125,
        331.2934265136719,
        336.9302978515625
      ],
      "text": "A\nHumans have an inborn ability to read and write.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.94461822509766,
        339.2095642089844,
        375.099609375,
        362.771728515625
      ],
      "text": "B_\nReading can be done using many different mediums.\nC\nWriting systems make unexpected demands on the brain.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.94461822509766,
        365.3780822753906,
        378.3967590332031,
        375.85595703125
      ],
      "text": "D_\nSome brain circuits adjust to whatever is required of them.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        49.06581497192383,
        390.8924255371094,
        377.5330810546875,
        401.37030029296875
      ],
      "text": "17.\nAccording to Mark Edmundson, the attitude of college students\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
